                <mxCell id="k4qvAeTSiCDNRpLVJHqQ-81" value="ALL complex actions have a defined max_duration. However, most CAs may effectively end earlier (scheduling idle for the remaining time). Since this is quite common, we see the possibility to have a deadline mechanism handled by the Core: a Core primitive lets you push deadlines to a stack, and another informs the Core that the CA is &quot;done&quot; until the deadline. As a result, the Core autonomously schedules idle slots.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=default;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontColor=light-dark(#FF0000,#FFFF00);" parent="1" vertex="1">
