                <mxCell id="k-lkDVU8fVcIlR1S431N-19" parent="o0cJBMDJHNSw0rVvinLR-1" style="shape=note2;boundedLbl=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=10;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;spacing=0;container=0;" value="&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;C:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;CA allocates buffers and decides whether to use GeneralPurpose or TightlyCoupled.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;It asks the RAL if it supports Tighlty Coupled, and allocates if actually wanted.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Benefits:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;- General Purpose -&amp;gt; simple implementations possible, RAL has to copy the data all the time&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;- Tightly Coupled -&amp;gt; might be used to improve perf&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;- Its lifecycle is managed by the RAL&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;- the decision on the buffer type will be static (not change during runtime)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- the lifecycle of the buffer is in the responsibility of the CA -- useful, you might want to keep data fro longer time, etc.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;====&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Side Question: after defining enter_range, commit, and leave: maybe having the buffer allocated at the RAL only?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;-- &amp;gt; thourgh this we might get limited with the physical space available in the radio&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="350" width="530" x="-4880" y="5390" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
